caseStudy:
  problem: "A premium product launch needs a page that feels as considered as the product. Flat photos and a spec list don't show how something is made, and heavy 3D sites are often slow on phones and invisible to Google."
  built: "A launch page where a real-time 3D model of the headphones is built in code and lit with physically based materials. Scrolling drives the camera, an exploded view of the parts and the finish colours. Phones get light pre-rendered stills first and only switch to WebGL when you interact; reduced-motion settings keep the still version. Every word is real HTML with structured data, so the page can still be found in search."
